WHY THE SOURCE IS PUBLIC

This program runs with administrator rights and updates itself. Anyone who
installs it should be able to read exactly what it does before trusting it,
and to check that the released binary matches the code it claims to be built
from. That is why the source is published. Publication is not a grant of
rights to reuse it.

WHAT YOU MAY DO

  - Read, study and audit this source code.
  - Build it yourself and run your own build on machines you control.
  - Report problems, and propose changes for inclusion in this project.

WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO WITHOUT PRIOR WRITTEN PERMISSION FROM THE COPYRIGHT HOLDER

  - Redistribute this source code, in whole or in part, modified or not.
  - Distribute binaries built from it.
  - Publish derivative works, or incorporate any part of this code into
    another project, whether free, commercial, internal or academic.
  - Use this code to train or fine-tune a machine learning model.
  - Remove or alter this notice, the authorship information, or the
    release-signature verification.

